What is Threads:
     - light-weight sub process that allows Java to perform multiple tasks simultaneously
     - normal start thread: Main

Without Threads:
    - one tasks must finish before another starts
    - Application slowness
    - UI Freeze

With Threads:
    - Multiple tasks run concurrently
    - Better performance
    - Better user experience

Process:
    - Independent program
    - Seperate memory
    - Heavyweight
    - slower

Threads:
    - part of process
    - Lightweight
    - Shared memory
    - Faster

Single Threaded Application:
    Cook takes care of
        - Taking order
        - Cooking
        - Billing
        - Packing

MultiThreading application:
    Server- Taking order
    Cook - cook food
    Billing counter -  Billing
    Package team - packing


Thread Lifecycle:
New-->Runnable-->Running-->waiting--Dead
